title Authenticated reference graph - scoped source accepted, operations unqualified

participant "tooling/reference-entrypoints.json\npackages/runtime/tests/fixtures/reference-sources.json" as PIN
participant "packages/runtime/tests/\nreference-bundles.test.ts" as GUARD
participant "Git cat-file\nlocal object database" as ODB
participant "Reference filesystem\nand stage-0 index" as PHYSICAL
participant "tooling/build-reference.ts" as BUILD

PIN -> GUARD: Independent SHA-1 commit pin
GUARD -> GUARD: Canonical top-level, SHA-1 format, original HEAD, no replacements
GUARD -> GUARD: Start 20-second graph deadline before commit retrieval
GUARD -> ODB: cat-file commit pin; no lazy fetch and no terminal prompt
ODB --> GUARD: Raw commit body, not a batch frame; bounded helper output
GUARD -> GUARD: Require SHA1(commit header + raw body) == independent pin; else fail immediately
note over GUARD, ODB
  An object pathname does not authenticate
  its contents. Validate commit and tree bodies
  before interpreting the pinned inventory.
end note
GUARD -> GUARD: Only then parse the first strict root-tree OID

loop breadth-first tree batches within graph budgets
  GUARD -> ODB: Request root / child OIDs from authenticated ancestry only
  ODB --> GUARD: OID / tree type / size / exact binary body / newline
  GUARD -> GUARD: Require framing and SHA1(tree header + body) == requested OID; else fail immediately
  GUARD -> GUARD: Decode strict modes and UTF-8 component names; reject duplicates
  GUARD -> GUARD: Reject empty / dot / dot-dot / separator names and unsupported modes
  GUARD -> GUARD: Cache verified nodes for this validation only
  note over GUARD
    Cache verified nodes without discarding paths.
    Expand a reused subtree beneath every parent
    so input membership remains complete.
  end note
  GUARD -> GUARD: Instantiate every parent path; enforce independent graph / path budgets
end

alt missing object, bad hash / framing / tree, or exhausted budget
  GUARD -> GUARD: Fail closed; no inventory trust, bundle build or import
  GUARD -> GUARD: Never fetch / invoke promisor helpers / scan history with fsck
else complete authenticated graph
  GUARD -> GUARD: Derive inventory from verified graph, never unauthenticated ls-tree
  GUARD -> PHYSICAL: Match raw blob Git SHA-1, executable mode and safe path kinds
  GUARD -> PHYSICAL: Exact stage-0 mode / OID / path set and H flags
  GUARD -> BUILD: Build only after source validation
  BUILD --> GUARD: Selected entries and all consumed input size / SHA-256 metadata
  GUARD -> PHYSICAL: Reauthenticate physical inputs after inventory capture
  GUARD -> GUARD: Require every consumed input's graph membership / size / SHA-256
  GUARD -> GUARD: Permit imports only after every retained check passes
end

legend
  Implemented source; 25 tests / 194 assertions pass, zero failures.
  One full C14 test remains filtered; no complete C14/native proof.
  TypeScript security and final adversarial packet-5 source scopes accepted.
  closure-reference-1 repeats 25/194; one C14 test remains filtered.
  Prior 16/108 evidence is PRE_OBJECT_GRAPH_AUTHENTICATION.
  4 MiB caps: metadata / batch stdin / cumulative tree I/O / path bytes.
  At most 4,096 cached trees and 16,384 instantiated entries.
  Tree depth <=32 from root 0; individual UTF-8 path <=4,096 bytes.
  Graph deadline 20s; helpers <=10s within remaining graph time.
  Physical blobs <=16 MiB each and <=128 MiB aggregate.
  GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1; GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0.
  Validator never invokes worktree/cached diff or clean/textconv.
  Corruption fixtures write only the owned clone, never shared alternates.
  Owned corruption/local-canary, parser, cache and graph-bound cases pass.
  Existing SHA-1 pin model; no collision-resistance upgrade.
  No atomic filesystem snapshot, full C14 proof or operational grant.
  Diagram rendering grants no operational authority.
endlegend
